vkd3d-proton: shader model 6.2+ from the real FP32 float controls.

Reverts the MoltenVK waiver of 0166. MoltenVK now reports FP32 denorm
preserve and flush-to-zero with 32-bit independence (0184), backed by the
SPIRV-Cross lowering of 0181/0183, so upstream's own condition promotes
SM 6.2 -> 6.3 -> 6.5 again without discarding a DXIL preserve request.

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/device.c b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
index 6541cac..700a495 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/device.c
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/device.c
@@ -9752,20 +9752,9 @@ static void d3d12_device_caps_init_shader_model(struct d3d12_device *device)
             }
         }
 
-        /* AnyOS: MoltenVK reports VK_SHADER_FLOAT_CONTROLS_INDEPENDENCE_NONE
-         * and no denorm preserve/flush support at all (Metal offers no
-         * per-shader denorm control), which would stop the shader model at
-         * 6.0 and reject every lib_6_3 DXIL library -- all of DXR -- before
-         * the ray tracing tier is even consulted.  The denorm execution
-         * modes are already dropped when the properties say unsupported
-         * (the same treatment as the NVIDIA exception above), so the
-         * shader model moves on without them. */
-        if (!denorm_behavior &&
-                device->device_info.vulkan_1_2_properties.driverID == VK_DRIVER_ID_MOLTENVK)
-        {
-            INFO("MoltenVK: no float-control independence; enabling SM 6.2+ without denorm modes.\n");
-            denorm_behavior = true;
-        }
+        /* AnyOS: no MoltenVK waiver. MoltenVK (0184) reports FP32 DenormPreserve
+         * and DenormFlushToZero with 32-bit independence because SPIRV-Cross
+         * (0181/0183) implements both modes, so the upstream gate above decides. */
 
         if (denorm_behavior)
         {
